1
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:12,400
Hello and welcome to this module which will introduce you to one of the key engineering

2
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:15,080
controls.

3
00:00:15,080 --> 00:00:22,080
Biological safety cabinets offer a safe working environment in which both the operator as

4
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:28,400
well as the sample are protected from extraneous contamination.

5
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:35,360
This biological safety cabinet must be utilized in accordance with the administrative control

6
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:41,320
for the standard operating procedures stated therein.

7
00:00:41,320 --> 00:00:47,240
Every biological safety cabinet must be certified periodically in compliance with your local

8
00:00:47,240 --> 00:00:51,960
regulatory authority or your national standards.

9
00:00:51,960 --> 00:00:58,380
A biological safety cabinet must be utilized in accordance with the standard operating

10
00:00:58,380 --> 00:01:03,760
procedure in order to achieve a safe and conducive working environment.

11
00:01:06,100 --> 00:01:12,140
As we proceed in this module, I will introduce you to the standard operating procedures for

12
00:01:12,140 --> 00:01:16,260
this particular biological safety cabinet.

13
00:01:16,260 --> 00:01:23,060
Please take note that the procedures may vary based on the manufacturer and you will have

14
00:01:23,060 --> 00:01:30,700
to develop your own standard operating procedures and validate them prior to commencing operations

15
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:37,900
in biological safety cabinets.

16
00:01:37,900 --> 00:01:44,820
In this video, I will be describing to you the layout of the standard biological safety

17
00:01:44,820 --> 00:01:46,580
cabinet.

18
00:01:46,580 --> 00:01:55,180
This cabinet is designed to protect both the sample as well as the operator from exposure

19
00:01:55,180 --> 00:01:59,460
to the biological agent.

20
00:01:59,460 --> 00:02:06,780
As you can see, all your equipment within this biological safety cabinet has to be laid

21
00:02:06,780 --> 00:02:13,500
out so as to ensure a smooth working environment.

22
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:18,860
These are the pipettes which are required for dispensing the samples which are located

23
00:02:18,860 --> 00:02:21,580
at this end.

24
00:02:21,580 --> 00:02:23,740
These are my pipette tips.

25
00:02:23,740 --> 00:02:30,740
This is the sample which will be transferred and finally over here I have the waste container.

26
00:02:30,740 --> 00:02:38,300
This waste container is specially designed for sharps and other disposable waste.

27
00:02:38,300 --> 00:02:45,820
For the purpose of our biological safety cabinet, pipette tips are considered as sharps

28
00:02:45,820 --> 00:02:48,780
and are disposed in this container.

29
00:02:48,780 --> 00:02:56,460
The container is filled to one-fourth of its level with a designated sterilant.

30
00:02:56,460 --> 00:03:00,060
In this case, I am using 70% ethanol.

31
00:03:00,060 --> 00:03:10,130
When we work, we generally work in a smooth flow.

32
00:03:10,130 --> 00:03:14,850
So as you can see, I am going to select the pipette.

33
00:03:14,850 --> 00:03:20,140
Then I install the pipette tip.

34
00:03:20,140 --> 00:03:33,530
I set the volume and I am going to withdraw this sample from this bottle and dispense

35
00:03:33,530 --> 00:03:47,770
it in the appropriate slot.

36
00:03:47,770 --> 00:03:54,810
This is a smooth operation of the entire process.

37
00:03:54,810 --> 00:04:09,570
When you complete dispensing the sample, the tips can be disposed in the waste container.

38
00:04:09,570 --> 00:04:16,590
There are some tips which one needs to note when working in this biological safety cabinet.

39
00:04:16,590 --> 00:04:23,930
This region basically has a downdraft of air which protects me as the operator from

40
00:04:23,930 --> 00:04:30,690
this sample as well as protects the sample from any kind of contamination which may be

41
00:04:30,690 --> 00:04:33,610
produced in the environment.

42
00:04:33,610 --> 00:04:39,330
Which is why we work within this zone.

43
00:04:39,330 --> 00:04:43,690
There are some things which you cannot do in a biological safety cabinet.

44
00:04:43,690 --> 00:04:50,390
For example, the usage of open flames is not permitted as the flame will generate a

45
00:04:50,390 --> 00:04:58,130
convection current which can disturb the flow of air in this biological safety cabinet.

46
00:04:58,130 --> 00:05:04,130
The second thing which you cannot do is operate centrifuges in this environment.

47
00:05:04,130 --> 00:05:11,730
As centrifuges have their own specific air flow patterns generated by their cooling motors

48
00:05:11,730 --> 00:05:16,610
and this can in turn disturb the air flow.

49
00:05:16,610 --> 00:05:20,690
These are some of the precautions which you need to take into consideration when working

50
00:05:20,690 --> 00:05:23,570
in a biological safety cabinet.

51
00:05:23,570 --> 00:05:32,010
Now biological safety cabinets must be decontaminated prior to use using a specified sterilizing

52
00:05:32,010 --> 00:05:43,990
agent as well as ultraviolet light and disinfected post usage by using the same sterilant with

53
00:05:43,990 --> 00:05:51,510
regard to clean up of this cabinet after use, please ensure that you dispose of this

54
00:05:51,510 --> 00:05:59,270
waste bin in a designated area and in accordance with the requisite standard operating procedure

55
00:05:59,270 --> 00:06:03,270
when it achieves a level which is two thirds full.

56
00:06:03,270 --> 00:06:09,570
This bin has to be sealed and disposed of according to the standard operating procedure

57
00:06:09,570 --> 00:06:15,290
which may involve autoclaving or incineration.

58
00:06:15,290 --> 00:06:23,170
These are some of the basic guidelines for utilizing a biological safety cabinet.

59
00:06:23,170 --> 00:06:30,530
Please refer to your own specific national and local guidelines when you need to develop

60
00:06:30,530 --> 00:06:35,730
your own standard operating procedures for biological safety cabinets.

61
00:06:35,730 --> 00:06:37,210
Thank you very much for watching.
